.TH EVENT_LOOP_CONSTRUCT 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
event_loop_construct \- declare and initialise an event_loop in one step
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

event_loop_construct(name, max_events_per_wait, num_lock_stripes,
                     num_reactor_threads);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Declares an event_loop variable named name, calls event_loop_create() to
initialise it, and calls fatal_err() if creation fails.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name                  Variable name for the event_loop handle.
max_events_per_wait   Size of the epoll_wait batch buffer each reactor
                      thread uses (must be between 1 and INT_MAX
                      inclusive, and small enough that
                      max_events_per_wait * sizeof(struct epoll_event)
                      does not overflow size_t).
num_lock_stripes      Number of independent lock stripes for the fd/entry
                      registry (must be >= 1).  1 means a single
                      shared lock.
num_reactor_threads   Number of background reactor threads (must be
                      >= 1; 1 means a single thread that both polls
                      and dispatches inline).
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Calls fatal_err() on failure; use event_loop_create() or
event_loop_create_with_mprocs() directly when graceful error handling
is required.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
event_loop_construct(loop, 32, 1, 1);
event_reg reg = event_loop_add(loop, selectable_from_fd(fd, ccol_select_read),
                                handlers, NULL, NULL);
event_loop_remove(loop, reg);
event_loop_destroy(loop);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR event_loop_construct_scoped (3),
.BR event_loop_declare (3),
.BR event_loop_create (3),
.BR event_loop_add (3),
.BR event_loop_destroy (3)
